The loader's error and warning counts, right end of row 3.

** Same helpers as the dashboard, no second source
`manifolding-dashboard/widgets/status' already reports these, from
`manifolding-emacs-errors-list' and `manifolding-emacs-warnings-list'. This
segment calls the same two functions rather than keeping its own tally, so
the bar and the dashboard cannot disagree about whether the config is clean.

** Nothing to detach
The design assumed a doctor segment already lived in `global-mode-string' and
would need moving out. It does not: there is no live mode-line configuration
anywhere in the tree — `global-mode-string' and `mode-line-format` appear
only in the Emacs manual extract at `the-screen/display/06-screen', which this
build migrated the mode-line chapters out of. So this is a new segment, not a
relocation, and no loader edit is involved.

** Segment
#+begin_src emacs-lisp
(defvar manifolding-modeline--doctor-cache nil
  "Cached doctor text, or nil when the config is clean and there is nothing to say.")

(defun manifolding-modeline--doctor-count (getter)
  "Length of the loader list GETTER returns, tolerating an absent loader."
  (if (fboundp getter)
      (length (funcall getter))
    0))

(defun manifolding-modeline--doctor-refresh ()
  "Recompute the doctor text. Shows nothing when there is nothing wrong."
  (let ((errors (manifolding-modeline--doctor-count
                 'manifolding-emacs-errors-list))
        (warnings (manifolding-modeline--doctor-count
                   'manifolding-emacs-warnings-list)))
    (setq manifolding-modeline--doctor-cache
          (cond ((> errors 0) (format "err %d" errors))
                ((> warnings 0) (format "warn %d" warnings))
                (t nil)))))

(manifolding-modeline-define-segment doctor
  :doc "Loader errors and warnings. Silent when clean."
  :face nil
  :side :right
  :construct
  (lambda ()
    (let ((text manifolding-modeline--doctor-cache))
      (and text
           ;; Errors and warnings share the red accent. Distinguishing them
           ;; by colour as well as by word would put a fourth accent in a
           ;; bar that promised three, for a difference the word already
           ;; makes.
           (list :propertize text (list 'face 'manifolding-modeline-alert)))))
  :refresh '(manifolding-modeline--doctor-refresh))
#+end_src

** Silent when clean
An empty right-hand cluster is what lets the bar read as one deliberate line
rather than a stub, so a healthy config deliberately shows nothing here
instead of "err 0". If you would rather always see the numbers, the
`t' branch in the refresh is the only thing to change.
